\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =2(-1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(0,-2).$" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275360 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275361 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275362 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275363 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275364 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1041 "selection" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275364 13194139533970 true] [17592186275359 1110 #uuid "481c26d6-c9ac-574d-b09d-88b872897a43" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275360 1034 "(0,1)" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275360 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275360 1111 #uuid "7125a0f6-71d4-5b67-88d0-a68f99c87a54" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275361 1034 "(0,2)" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275361 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275361 1111 #uuid "e9af544b-466b-58e9-a32d-a60c65ebd92a" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275362 1034 "(2,0)" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275362 1111 #uuid "c13b32c5-aed0-5095-8fe9-48fd28fb9b50" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275363 1034 "(-2,0)" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275363 1111 #uuid "bb6363fb-0afc-5a52-bb45-6b4949cde79c" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275364 1034 "(0,-2)" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275364 1111 #uuid "cdef4042-cff9-5f68-95fb-b34786a01c9c" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275365 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275366 13194139533970 true] [17592186275365 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275368 13194139533970 true] [17592186275365 1089 "q-276807" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275365 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533970 true] [17592186275365 1100 "The point $A$ has polar coordinates $(r,\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ and the point $B$ has polar coordinates $(2r,\\frac{7\\pi }{6}).$ Determine the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ given that the Cartesian coordinates of $A$ are $(2\\sqrt{3},2).$\n\nThe Cartesian coordinates of $B$ are $(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275365 1113 #uuid "918774b9-5070-53eb-909c-a82fbf0008b2" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275365 1145 "First, we use the Cartesian coordinates of $A$ to find $r,$ the distance between $A$ and the origin:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the polar coordinates of $B$ are\n\n$$\n(2\\cdot 4,\\frac{7\\pi }{6})=(8,\\frac{7\\pi }{6}).\n$$\n\nNow, we convert $B$ to Cartesian coordinates. To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ are $(-4\\sqrt{3},-4).$" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275367 13194139533970 true] [17592186275366 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533970 true] [17592186275366 1041 "field-1" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275366 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275367 13194139533970 true] [17592186275366 1110 #uuid "83c9261d-ccd7-5cdc-a6a8-909f279e1fc7" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275367 1034 "-4\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275367 1111 #uuid "5b33ecd2-5729-5a5a-8169-3cfb91b5d454" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275369 13194139533970 true] [17592186275368 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533970 true] [17592186275368 1041 "field-2" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275368 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275369 13194139533970 true] [17592186275368 1110 #uuid "93afe242-8f69-50d6-8f5a-1b5d3fc06931" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275369 1034 "-4" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275369 1111 #uuid "46242961-b667-5d61-8860-6d07deada67a" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275370 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275371 13194139533970 true] [17592186275370 1089 "q-40804" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275370 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533970 true] [17592186275370 1100 "The point $A$ has polar coordinates $(r,\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$ and the point $B$ has polar coordinates $({r}^{2},\\frac{4\\pi }{3}).$ Find the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ given that the Cartesian coordinates of $A$ are $(-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}).$" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275370 1113 #uuid "4ec897fc-4ba3-5ac8-96c6-00d8646f2622" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275370 1145 "First, we use the Cartesian coordinates of $A$ to find $r,$ the distance between $A$ and the origin:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the polar coordinates of $B$ are\n\n$$\n((\\sqrt{10})^{2},\\frac{4\\pi }{3})=(10,\\frac{4\\pi }{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we convert $B$ to Cartesian coordinates. To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =10(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =10(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ are $(-5,-5\\sqrt{3}).$" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275372 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275373 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275374 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275375 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275376 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1041 "selection" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275374 13194139533970 true] [17592186275371 1110 #uuid "6e9b9746-ed79-5873-ae10-e6ef08710927" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275372 1034 "(-\\sqrt{5},-3\\sqrt{5})" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275372 1111 #uuid "a980a14f-459e-537f-a11c-99b093b3b3e7" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275373 1034 "(-5\\sqrt{3},-5)" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275373 1111 #uuid "aae262cc-5056-59b4-b6e1-ab8ae0dce2bc" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275374 1034 "(-5,-5\\sqrt{3})" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [17592186275374 1111 #uuid "2962a42e-9c54-5089-bfd7-049df8d04250" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275375 1034 "(-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{15})" 13194139533970 true] [17592186275375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533970 true] [1759218627537